				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is a beautiful young East Asian female singer based on the female visual identity, composition, lighting, and styling language from <Picture 1>, the image-node template reference. She has elegant facial features, long dark hair moving naturally in the wind, expressive eyes, refined makeup, and a graceful cinematic presence. Her outfit follows the template image's overall fashion silhouette and color harmony, adapted into a soft oatmeal-and-blue-gray travel-inspired costume with a light scarf. Preserve her face, hairstyle, body proportions, costume design, and visual identity throughout the video.\n<Audio 1> is the original music track “思念故乡”, used as the synchronized singing, emotional, and rhythmic reference for the target video.\n<Picture 1> is the image-node template reference. Preserve its visual composition, lighting direction, color palette, framing language, fashion styling, and cinematic atmosphere while replacing the original subject with <Subject 1>.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reuse] The target video is a 10-second cinematic music-video performance featuring <Subject 1>, a beautiful female singer. <Picture 1> provides the required image-node template style and visual structure. The first 10 seconds of <Audio 1> are reused as the complete soundtrack, and <Subject 1> sings along naturally with accurate lip-sync, breath timing, facial emotion, and body movement.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4]): fully_preserved - preserve the same beautiful female face, hairstyle, costume, body proportions, singing identity, and graceful emotional performance throughout.\n<Picture 1> (template reference): fully_preserved - retain its composition, lighting, color palette, camera language, styling logic, and atmosphere while adapting the subject into a female singer.\n<Audio 1>: partially_copy - reuse the first 10 seconds of <Audio 1> as the complete final audio track, preserving its original melody, rhythm, vocal phrasing, and emotional progression.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic cinematic music video based on the visual template from <Picture 1>. Preserve the template's framing, lighting direction, color harmony, camera rhythm, and fashion atmosphere. The main subject is always the same beautiful female singer. She must visibly sing along to <Audio 1> with accurate mouth shapes, natural breathing, subtle jaw and throat movement, expressive eyes, and emotionally believable vocal performance. Do not invent lyrics or add spoken dialogue.\n\n[Shot 1] At 00:00.000, use the template image's opening composition and visual atmosphere. A wide cinematic shot shows <Subject 1> standing on an old rural train platform at dusk, positioned according to the template's main subject placement. Her long dark hair and light scarf move gently in the wind. She begins singing immediately with the opening vocal phrase of <Audio 1>, using restrained emotion and a soft, breathy delivery. The camera makes a slow forward dolly.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.300, cut using the template's established framing language to a medium side-profile shot. <Subject 1> continues singing in perfect sync with <Audio 1>. Her eyes look toward the distant railway horizon, and her expression conveys longing for home. She lightly touches the scarf near her chest while singing. Keep the gesture elegant and minimal.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:04.800, move into a close-up and then an extreme close-up of her face. Clearly show her lips articulating the sung melody, natural breath pauses, subtle facial muscle movement, moist expressive eyes, and delicate emotional changes. She looks slightly toward the camera while continuing to sing. The camera performs a slow micro push-in during the musical emotional rise.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:07.200, cut to a rear three-quarter tracking shot matching the template's visual rhythm. <Subject 1> walks slowly beside fields and old houses while continuing to sing. Her voice remains synchronized with <Audio 1>; her posture is graceful and controlled. The camera follows at shoulder height.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:09.300, return to a close-up framed according to the template image. In warm sunset rim light, <Subject 1> completes the final sung phrase within the 10-second excerpt. She finishes with a restrained bittersweet smile and a lingering gaze toward the distance. End at 00:10.000 on her eyes and fading sunset light.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nReuse the first 10 seconds of <Audio 1> as the dominant soundtrack. Add only subtle wind, distant train ambience, scarf movement, and quiet footsteps, mixed below the original music. The female singing must remain clear and synchronized with the original vocal or melody.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\n<Audio 1> is directly reused as the audience-only music and singing reference. Preserve its original tempo, melody, vocal phrasing, emotional contour, instrumentation, and timing. <Subject 1> must visibly perform the song rather than silently lip-syncing without expression. Do not add new lyrics, another singer, spoken dialogue, subtitles, or unrelated music.",
